Subject: installer: install only the helper this package pins
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local policy; upstream installs and updates the newest helper it downloads]
Drop-when: upstream stops replacing the helper with a downloaded binary

Upstream's customize.sh, action.sh and susfs-bin-update.sh download
ksu_susfs from sidex15/susfs4ksu-binaries and install it if it runs, and
susfs-bin-check.sh compares the installed helper with that download.
This package ships the helper CI compiles from the kernel's own SUSFS
commit instead. The installer requires driver 40900 and SUSFS v2.3.0,
checks the helper against @KSU_SUSFS_SHA256@ (export-dist.py fills in
the digest) and no longer copies sus_su, which SUSFS 2.x dropped and
this package does not ship. The action shows the SUSFS version and
features; the update script refuses to run.
